Day 1: APIM fundamentals
- Understand APIs, operations, backends, products and subscriptions
- Explain the request lifecycle and gateway versus management plane

Day 2: Policies and routing
- Practice inbound, backend, outbound and on-error policies
- Create a backend mapping and a URL rewrite example

Day 3: API security
- Study OAuth 2.0, JWT, Entra ID, mTLS and subscription keys
- Practice token validation and managed identity concepts

Day 4: Networking
- Draw Application Gateway → APIM → private backend
- Review DNS, TLS, private endpoints, routing and NSG/firewall troubleshooting

Day 5: MuleSoft migration
- Build an API inventory template and capability mapping
- Explain gateway-only versus integration-runtime migration

Day 6: Terraform and CI/CD
- Plan APIM infrastructure as code
- Design a pipeline for API definitions and policies across environments

Day 7: Hands-on APIM
- Import a sample OpenAPI API
- Configure a policy and test successful and unsuccessful requests

Day 8: Key Vault and identity
- Configure a secure certificate or secret reference in a test environment
- Review managed identity, RBAC and rotation

Day 9: Troubleshooting and monitoring
- Practice 401, 403, 429, 502 and 504 scenarios
- Review metrics, diagnostics, alerts and correlation IDs

Day 10: Availability and performance
- Study capacity, throttling, caching and timeout considerations
- Explain recovery and multi-region design trade-offs

Day 11: Logic Apps and Functions
- Learn orchestration versus custom code
- Map common Mule flows to Azure integration options

Day 12: Messaging and B2B
- Compare Service Bus, Event Grid and Event Hubs
- Review Integration Accounts, EDI and partner integration

Day 13: Mock migration design
- Design a phased migration of 100–200 APIs
- Include network, security, automation, testing and rollback

Day 14: Mock interview
- Answer the 12 questions without notes
- Present an architecture diagram and defend your design choices